2. BUILDER-SUPPLIED    visibly self-reported

CLAIM_BEING_EVALUATED       SECTION 4A WAS WRONG IN THE FIRST DRAFT AND IS CORRECTED IN PLACE. It said to wire assert_chain_closed into the gate. Measured: that check refuses ('P1','P2'), which is the state every legitimate run is in before it starts, so wiring it would refuse every legitimate run. ChainResolution.closed cannot separate a pre-start P2 chain from an abandoned P3 chain either — both are False.
KNOWN_FAILURES
  THE PREVIOUS DELIVERY OF THIS PROPOSAL WAS REJECTED_INCOMPLETE by a fresh Sol, origin BUILDER, cause SOURCE_CONTENT: I handed over the bare file with no Review Packet and no declared SHA-256. That reviewer was correct to stop. This packet is the remedy, and the reviewed set is the one that reviewer specified.
  That reviewer independently computed the proposal's hash as 7557AD42...60D5D; recomputed here it matches byte for byte. The file was never in doubt — the transport around it was absent.
KNOWN_ASSUMPTIONS           The replacement criterion is ABANDONED(chain) == last in {P3} union NON_TERMINAL_TRAPS, derived from the measured successor sets rather than from closure.
UNRESOLVED_UNCERTAINTIES
  P4: sealed and awaiting verification. Not abandoned, but should it permit new work on the same supplement_id? A second refusal reason, or not this gate's business?
  F2: post-start failure whose only successor is F3. May the same id run again? My read is no, but F2 is not in NON_TERMINAL_TRAPS so the vocabulary does not say so.
  Whether CR1 belongs in NON_TERMINAL_TRAPS. This is the builder's inference from shape-isomorphism with AX, not part of any ruling.
  Whether predecessors=(P3,) is too narrow — what happens to a crash after P4, or after A1?
COUNTERFACTUAL              If ABANDONED is judged wrong, the fallback is to define no gate predicate at all and leave the dangling-P3 refusal entirely to the amendment's bootstrap check — which means a dangling P3 keeps passing A_PRECHECK until the amendment lands.
BUILDER_RECOMMENDATION      Read section 4A first and treat it as the section most likely to still contain an error; the builder already overturned its first version there.

3. REVIEWER CONTRACT   what the reviewer is asked to do, and must not do

REVIEWER_TASK           discretionary phase-boundary review; it releases no transition and is never a requirement's gate
MUST_NOT_DO
  author
  repair
  approve its own prior work
  accept a summary in place of bytes
  treat a DECLARED, BUILDER, or SELECTED field as verified
  accept a narrowed Tier-2 base
  read UNKNOWN provenance as reviewer_only
  claim unscoped independence (INV-8)
REQUIRED_OUTPUT_SCHEMA
  VERDICT: PASS | HOLD | REJECTED_INCOMPLETE  (§5.5.2, its sole normative site; this HOLD is a different field from TRANSITION_ELIGIBILITY's HOLD)
  STRONGEST_OBJECTION: the best case against passing, stated even on PASS
  PATHS_PULLED: every path whose bytes were read — the actual paths, listed individually. A count is not a substitute
  INDEPENDENCE_STATEMENT: scoped per dimension and per target (QROS §3.1)
    INDEPENDENCE_UNKNOWN=YES — the affected certification must be reported as scoped-unknown or explicitly non-independent, or the separate certification obtained must be named
  ON a rejection verdict, additionally:
    REJECTION_ORIGIN_CLASS: vocabulary source [TBL-PACKET-ORIGINS]
    REJECTION_CAUSE_CLASS: RUNTIME_MECHANICAL_DEFECT | SOURCE_CONTENT | REVIEWER_DISCRETION | OTHER
PULL_PROTOCOL           the reviewer lists the paths it needs; the working session supplies verbatim bytes; refusal or inability to supply ⇒ a rejection verdict

